{
  "_about": [
    "Hand-written ground truth for a stratified sample of the Red Herring Prospectus.",
    "Each record names a source paragraph by its position in the document's paragraph",
    "stream (`index`) and by its opening text (`anchor`). build_gold.py reads the .docx,",
    "checks the anchor against the indexed paragraph, and resolves these labels to",
    "character offsets -- so the labels below are the only hand-authored part, a",
    "transcription error is impossible, and a label that is not present verbatim fails",
    "the build loudly.",
    "",
    "Labelling policy (mirrors README, 'Precision choices we made deliberately'):",
    "  * Company/registration identifiers (CIN, SEBI registration no., firm registration",
    "    no.) are NOT PII - they identify a filing, not a person.",
    "  * Names of regulators and exchanges (SEBI, BSE, NSE, Registrar of Companies) are NOT",
    "    labelled as ORGANIZATION; they are public bodies, not private parties.",
    "  * A paragraph is labelled ADDRESS when it carries a street-level locator (plot,",
    "    building, village, street) OR a postal code. Word stores each table cell and each",
    "    line as its own paragraph, so a single postal address is often split across two or",
    "    three of them; each part that meets the rule is labelled separately.",
    "  * A paragraph holding only a state and/or country ('Maharashtra, India') is NOT an",
    "    address, and a bare city name is not either.",
    "  * A designation ('Independent Director') is not PII; the person's name is.",
    "  * 'occurrence' is 1-based and defaults to 1; whitespace in 'text' matches flexibly."
  ],
